Anduril Industries is a defense technology company with a mission to transform U.S. and allied military capabilities with advanced technology. By bringing the expertise, technology, and business model of the 21st century’s most innovative companies to the defense industry, Anduril is changing how military systems are designed, built and sold. Anduril’s family of systems is powered by Lattice OS, an AI-powered operating system that turns thousands of data streams into a realtime, 3D command and control center. As the world enters an era of strategic competition, Anduril is committed to bringing cutting-edge autonomy, AI, computer vision, sensor fusion, and networking technology to the military in months, not years.

ABOU T THE TEAM

Anduril's Imaging business line designs and builds state-of-the-art imaging systems, deployed to tackle the most significant security challenges of America and its allies. Advanced Infrared Solutions operates out of our Hudson, NH location, focused on the design and manufacturing of high-performance cooled infrared cameras and Integrated Dewar Cooler Assemblies (IDCAs) that encompass Imaging products. Advanced Infrared Solutions supplies these critical components both internally to Imaging products, and externally as a merchant supplier to the broader defense, space, and commercial industrial base. &nbsp;

ABOUT THE JOB &nbsp;

As the R&amp;D Engineering Technician, you will collaborate closely with development and test engineers to create and evaluate innovative optical systems for various platforms, including airborne, maritime, and space applications. You will be responsible for fabricating high-quality electro-mechanical assemblies and managing the rapid prototyping process, ensuring all projects are executed efficiently and effectively. Additionally, your expertise in troubleshooting and assembly will be crucial as you oversee internal prototyping resources and support external testing initiatives. The Anduril Imaging business line is developing infrared camera systems at the highest priority level designated by the Department of War. This role will be directly working with the engineering team and be crucial to the success of these development efforts.&nbsp; &nbsp;

WHAT YOU’LL DO: &nbsp;

• Work closely with development and test engineers to build and test new infrared optical systems for airborne, maritime and space platforms &nbsp;

• Fabricate and assemble high quality, high reliability and electro-mechanical assemblies. &nbsp;

• Develop and implement integration and test fixtures; setup and use existing test equipment, monitor, and report the results. &nbsp;

• Own internal prototyping resources, including mechanical and electrical fabrication equipment &nbsp;

• Manage R+D space from a facilities and organizational standpoint &nbsp;

• Travel to external laboratories and test sites as needed. &nbsp;

REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS:

• 10+ years of experience as an electro-mechanical technician working on high-precision micro-assemblies, vacuum systems, or wafer-handling equipment. &nbsp;

• Rapid Prototyping Ownership: Proven ability to manage R&amp;D builds from concept to completion with minimal oversight-including sourcing components, assembling, testing, and troubleshooting. &nbsp;

• Electrical Fundamentals: Strong working knowledge of basic electrical principles (e.g., Ohm’s Law, calculating voltage drop, sizing wire gauges based on current/amperage). &nbsp;

• Harness &amp; Cable Fabrication: Hands-on experience building, routing, and troubleshooting custom wiring harnesses and power cables, including precision soldering, pin crimping, and connector assembly. &nbsp;

• Process Documentation: Ability to document assembly workflows, redline engineering drawings, and draft initial Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs) from a technician's viewpoint. &nbsp;

• Work Environment: Comfortable wearing full cleanroom attire (gown, mask, gloves) and following strict ESD-control protocols. &nbsp;

